@@ -1,5 +1,26 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## DexLab local worker inertial-precision fix
+
+- Preserve compiled mass, COM and diagonal inertia/frame at float64 round-trip precision in worker MJCF transport. Inferred and full-tensor inertias become explicit diagonal inertials after XML serialization; native SDK precision remains unchanged. This is a local adapter fix, not an engine change or upstream release.
+
+## DexLab local compliant-contact adapter extension
+
+- Add explicit paired stiffness/damping options for native force-based PhysX compliant contact. Author all bound collision materials before reset with average combination; read composed USD values back and reject missing/mixed semantics. Values are per native constraint, not whole-object material moduli. Defaults and official engines are unchanged. This is not an upstream UniSim release.
+
+## DexLab local contact diagnostics extension
+
+- Added explicit single-environment rigid-object normal-contact and friction-anchor snapshots. Poll every physics substep, preserve body identities, reject malformed/saturated buffers, and copy shared native counts before subsequent queries. Native collision exclusion relationships are exposed in diagnostic metadata. Official engine sources remain unchanged; this is not an upstream UniSim release.
+
+## DexLab local SDF adapter extension
+
+- Preserve mesh-backed MJCF SDF intent, import through a sibling mesh transport, and author/audit native PhysX SDF collision. Version cache identities; test optional slot alignment and unsupported input rejection. This is an adapter-only extension, not an upstream UniSim release.
+
+
+## Unreleased — DexLab adapter extension
+
+- Added opt-in `isaacsim_external_forces_every_iteration`, native scene authoring and strict boolean readback. Defaults are unchanged; official PhysX binaries are unchanged.
+
 ## 1.7.10 - 2026-09-24
 
 - Sped up mapped IsaacSim prototype authoring at catalog scale (1200-variant INIT entity build drops from 134s to 11s; total INIT from 158s to 35s). Two serialized overheads dominated: each per-variant prototype spawn went through IsaacLab's `UsdFileCfg` spawner, whose `check_usd_path_with_timeout` runs an asyncio `omni.client.stat_async` availability probe with a fixed ~0.1s event-loop yield per call (127s of the 157s INIT, at near-zero CPU/GPU utilization), and every spawn ran with the physics change listener attached, so PhysX parsed each transient prototype subtree (~43ms per variant) even though prototypes are removed before physics starts. The worker now authors the same reference arc directly through `isaacsim.core.utils.prims.create_prim` behind a plain `os.path.isfile` guard — every spawned path is a validated cache artifact (manifest + SHA-256) or a fresh copy of one, and every spawner override the worker set was `None` or unconsumed by the from-files spawner — and prototype spawns join the destination copies and the prototype scope removal under the existing single change-listener toggle, so physics only ever parses the final per-environment destinations. Stage-object edits stay outside the copy loop's `Sdf.ChangeBlock` (deferred layer notices break `DefinePrim` recomposition). Authored prims, the composed stage, PhysX view order, and the native instance audit are unchanged.
@@ -385,3 +406,7 @@
 - Bootstrap the `unisim` namespace and `unisim-core` distribution.
 - Add the backend-neutral `SimBackend` contract, fake backend, and conformance helper.
 - Reserve benchmark case/result interfaces without implementing workloads or measurements.
+
+### Local explicit torsional radius extension
+
+- Add opt-in minimum torsional contact radius with fail-closed host/worker validation and native USD readback; defaults and cached roles unchanged. This exposes an official PhysX parameter, not a solver patch.
